(6869674, 1034263, 89220, '<td valign="top">I agree with you <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=137576" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Giles_uk</a> on the creative part. Its not a new thing I tried. I just wanted to try this for this challenge. Thanks for the frank opinion. I also had doubt on the approval of SC and submitted the original along with my entry when I entered into this challenge.  I''ve seen similar cloning out methods got approved. Anyway, fingers crossed.</td>', 'I agree with you  Giles_uk on the creative part. Its not a new thing I tried. I just wanted to try this for this challenge. Thanks for the frank opinion. I also had doubt on the approval of SC and submitted the original along with my entry when I entered into this challenge.  I''ve seen similar cloning out methods got approved. Anyway, fingers crossed.', '2012-09-26 04:09:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6869715, 1034241, 137576, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Art Roflmao:</b></div><hr/><i> Well I gave it a 10, but since you mentioned she was your EX girlfriend, I''m deducting 4 points - show me a pic of your new girlfriend and I might give them back. :P (kidding, I gave it a 6)<br/> <br/>If you want a real critique from me, here it is: Obviously I was not put off by the gratuitous skinnage - the lighting is excellent, but there is something off-putting about the angle or perspective. Also, a shallower dof or more distance from that bkg might have improved it. As for the challenge topic - I would guess more voters saw this as just a gratuitous shoehorn-ish entry. That''s my take on it, FWIW. Don''t let these results eat at ya - there is nothing you can do about it and you KNOW many have tried. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>it doesnt bother me really just dont want dpc to become sterile conservative and safe like its heading, i like edgy and out there<br/> <br/>trust me this was not a shoe horn but the first thing that came ino my head would have violated the non naughty bits rule, and she was up for it, shes a bonny lass ;) <br/> <br/>just prefer people to say : vote: 1 : I" dont like to see women in underwear" or this is to suggestive etc but ppl dont which is a shame, <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Art Roflmao: Well I gave it a 10, but since you mentioned she was your EX girlfriend, I''m deducting 4 points - show me a pic of your new girlfriend and I might give them back. :P (kidding, I gave it a 6) If you want a real critique from me, here it is: Obviously I was not put off by the gratuitous skinnage - the lighting is excellent, but there is something off-putting about the angle or perspective. Also, a shallower dof or more distance from that bkg might have improved it. As for the challenge topic - I would guess more voters saw this as just a gratuitous shoehorn-ish entry. That''s my take on it, FWIW. Don''t let these results eat at ya - there is nothing you can do about it and you KNOW many have tried. :)   it doesnt bother me really just dont want dpc to become sterile conservative and safe like its heading, i like edgy and out there trust me this was not a shoe horn but the first thing that came ino my head would have violated the non naughty bits rule, and she was up for it, shes a bonny lass ;)  just prefer people to say : vote: 1 : I" dont like to see women in underwear" or this is to suggestive etc but ppl dont which is a shame,  ', '2012-09-26 04:52:58.000000', NULL, 0),
